    "rule": "Input RF clears at instruction entry. IRETD/IRETQ restore RF from the stack; word IRET does not."
  },
  "implementation": {
    "domain": "V5 SYSRET and inheriting profiles, V6 IRET/RETF and V7 SYSENTER/SYSEXIT accept RF, every IOPL and VIF/VIP. Input TF remains unowned. Invalid VM/reserved flags and earlier-profile requirements remain rejected.",
    "word_iret": "Retain AC/ID/VIF/VIP, clear input RF and replace low FLAGS from the word frame.",
    "other_returns": "Wider IRET restores RF from the frame; RETF and SYSEXIT clear RF; SYSENTER clears RF/IF/VM. SYSRET retains its existing defined R11 mask.",
    "prior_record_correction": "The narrow-frame record described word IRET as retaining RF. That general statement was incorrect; the previously qualified domain required input RF=0. This record explicitly supersedes that RF detail and qualifies RF=1 without rewriting historical evidence."
  },
